' SIS #02 — your FINAL sequence diagram goes here, as PlantUML (@startuml … @enduml).
' Start from the AI's original in models/original/sequence.puml, apply your accepted review
' decisions, then render it to models/img/sequence.png (or .svg). README section 5.
@startuml
autonumber
actor Student
participant "CatalogController" as CC
participant "EnrollmentService" as ES
database "Database / Repository" as DB

== R1: Catalog Browsing & Offering Selection ==
Student -> CC: browseCatalog(semester)
activate CC
CC -> DB: fetchCourseOfferings(semester)
activate DB
DB --> CC: return course offerings list
deactivate DB
CC --> Student: display catalog with offerings
deactivate CC

Student -> CC: selectCourseOffering(offeringId)
activate CC
CC --> Student: offering selected
deactivate CC

== R2, R3, R4, R5: Guarded Registration & Atomic Operation ==
Student -> ES: requestEnrollment(studentId, offeringId)
activate ES

note right of ES
  Final checks & enrollment creation 
  execute as one atomic transaction.
end note

ES -> DB: beginTransaction()
activate DB
ES -> DB: fetchCurrentOfferingData(offeringId)
DB --> ES: return current capacity, enrollment count, & student enrollments

note over ES
  EnrollmentService evaluates duplicate and 
  current-capacity conditions using repository data.
end note

alt already enrolled
    ES -> DB: rollbackTransaction()
    deactivate DB
    ES --> Student: reject: "already enrolled" (count unchanged)

else course full
    ES -> DB: rollbackTransaction()
    deactivate DB
    ES --> Student: reject: "course full" (count unchanged)

else not enrolled and places left
    ES -> DB: createEnrollment(studentId, offeringId)
    ES -> DB: incrementEnrollmentCount(offeringId)
    ES -> DB: commitTransaction()
    deactivate DB
    ES --> Student: return enrollment confirmation
end

deactivate ES
@enduml